WEBVTT

00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:04.455
Team! This is the Upgrade Quote Sheet.

00:00:04.495 --> 00:00:07.455
It turns a $5 upgrade into real money,

00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:09.495
for your customer and for you.

00:00:09.535 --> 00:00:12.855
It's live right now on
cookcountycooks.com.

00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:14.165
Let's go!

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.990
Step 1.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.300
Before we talk phones,

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.270
pull up the customer's core
account and hunt for leverage.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.450
Find every discount you can.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.360
Top box.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.610
What they pay today.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:25.760
$135.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.040
Next box.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.230
What they'll pay after
we make the changes.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.340
$95.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.480
Boom!

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.170
$40 a month in savings and we
haven't even touched a phone.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.530
That's your leverage.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.610
Step 2.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.850
Type in their current cell phone bill.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:41.980
$123.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.085
Done!

00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:44.275
Step 3.

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:45.775
Pick the phone they want.

00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:47.835
iPhone 18 Pro Max.

00:00:47.985 --> 00:00:49.355
And don't stop at one!

00:00:49.405 --> 00:00:53.295
You can quote 2, 3, even 5
phones on the same sheet.

00:00:53.365 --> 00:00:54.685
The more phones we quote,

00:00:54.725 --> 00:00:58.135
the more we save the customer
and the more leverage we build.

00:00:59.062 --> 00:01:00.352
Now look up top.

00:01:00.462 --> 00:01:04.472
That green number is your running
savings tally, monthly and yearly.

00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:07.032
Everything you add to
this sheet moves it.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.030
Step 4. The trade-in.
Upgrading to an iPhone?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.270
It's a dropdown.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.770
Find their phone,
pick the condition, done.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.880
Any other phone?

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.510
Look up the real trade-in
value and type it in.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.890
Here's how the math works.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.470
An upgrade credit, something like $200,

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.710
plus whatever the trade-in is worth.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.780
Look at that!

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.950
Their trade-in covers the whole phone.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.450
$1,300 down to zero.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.690
$76 a month in savings.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.980
Step 5. Build the bundle.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:38.030
First, set the membership tier,

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:42.320
because right now Diamond
customers get $300 off wearables.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.140
Today's customer is Silver.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.600
Now add a watch.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:49.060
Start with the lowest price,
the Apple Watch SE 3.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.720
$18.33 a month, line fee included.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:00.080
Now look at the green, $58 a month,
$693 a year, a brand new iPhone,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.700
a brand new Apple Watch and the

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.170
customer still pays $58
less every single month.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.560
Now hit View Customer
Preview and present it.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.590
Top box first.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.250
Left side. One phone, $1,299.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.310
Right side. The phone
and the watch, $299.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.130
Then the bottom box.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.070
Their bill today, $294.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.990
With the bundle, $236.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.310
Now let the customer decide.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.690
Build it right and they pick the
bundle on the right every single time.

00:02:30.938 --> 00:02:32.248
Saving them a lot?

00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:34.067
Then you have room to add more.

00:02:34.118 --> 00:02:39.368
Add a tablet. Phone, watch and iPad,
and they are still saving $21 a month.

00:02:39.438 --> 00:02:42.107
So find the need. The kids? Work?

00:02:42.238 --> 00:02:42.877
Fitness?

00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:44.507
Build the bundle around it.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.410
Why does this matter?

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.450
For the customer, it's value.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.900
They came in for a phone.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.030
They leave with a phone,
a watch and a lower bill.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.830
We're presenting the bundle,
not just the upgrade.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.700
And for you? An upgrade
by itself pays $5.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.080
A watch pays $10. A tablet pays $11.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:07.820
Same customer, same conversation,
and $5 just became $26.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.420
Now add accessories.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:10.890
You make 20%.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:14.450
$100 in accessories puts
another $20 in your pocket.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.380
That's $46 instead of $5.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.120
So here's the play.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:21.480
Find the leverage.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.960
Build the bundle. Show the savings.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.440
Let the customer choose.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.980
Use the Upgrade Quote Sheet
on every single upgrade.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.500
Now let's go cook!

